                        # Therefore, in a proper coloring, neighbors of v cannot have color target_color (same as v) nor color c (checked). So after swap, neighbors that were target_color become c, but since they were not adjacent to v? Wait, they are adjacent to v and had color target_color -> same as v, which is invalid. So in a proper coloring, this cannot happen.
                        # Hence, in a proper coloring, the component containing v of colors {c, target_color} will not include any neighbor of v except v itself? Actually, neighbors of v cannot be target_color (same color) nor c (by choice). So they are not in the component.
                        # Therefore, swapping the component is safe: v will become c, and no neighbor of v will become c (because neighbors are not in the component).
