                # After swap, v would get color c if it's in the component. But we need to ensure no conflict.
                # Actually, swapping colors in a Kempe chain preserves validity.
                # We can swap if after swap, v gets color c (i.e., v is in the component) and we don't introduce conflict? 
                # Swapping is safe. The point is to free target_color at v by moving it to c.
                # If we swap the component, v's color flips: if it was target_color, becomes c; if it was c, becomes target_color.
                # We want v to end up with color c, so we need v to be in the component and currently have target_color.
                if coloring[v] == target_color and v in component:
                    # Perform swap: flip c <-> target_color in component
                    for node in component:
                        if coloring[node] == c:
                            coloring[node] = target_color
                        elif coloring[node] == target_color:
